course: dictionary
lesson: 13118
title: Words for people and places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A florist is a person whose job is to sell and arrange flowers. The same word can also name a shop, so «the florist's» is the place where you buy flowers.
explain: Look at the ending of florist. Many words ending in -ist name a person who does a job, like dentist or artist. Say the word and think about who is doing the job.
explain: «Mum went to the florist to buy a bunch of tulips for Grandma's birthday.» Here the florist is the person, or the shop, who sold the tulips. To check, swap in a meaning: a person or a flower shop, and see which one makes sense.
explain: When you meet a word that could mean a person or a place, read the rest of the sentence. The words around it will tell you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: A florist is a noun, so you can have one florist or many florists.
fact: «Florist» means a person who sells and arranges flowers.
fact: «The florist's» means the shop where flowers are sold.
fact: A bouquet is a bunch of flowers arranged together, often as a present.
fact: Florists are often busy on birthdays, on Mother's Day, and when someone needs cheering up after being ill.
exercise: «The florist wrapped the roses in pink paper.» Who wrapped the roses? | *A florist | A nurse | A baker
exercise: «A florist has 4 bunches of 6 roses each.» How many roses are there in total? | 46 | *24 | 10
exercise: «The florist's window was full of red and yellow tulips.» What does florist's mean here? | A person who grows vegetables | A type of flower | *A flower shop
test: «Sara works as a florist on the high street.» What is a florist? | *A person who sells and arranges flowers | A person who looks after horses | A person who fixes cars
test: «Each bouquet costs 8 pounds. A florist sells 5 bouquets.» How many pounds does the florist get in total? | 35 | *40 | 45 | 13
exam: «The florist's shop was closed on Sunday, so Dad bought the flowers on Saturday.» Which word names a place? | Saturday | Dad | *florist's | bought
